\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Therefore, the parametric equations are:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=7-3t \\\\ y=-11+2t \\\\ z=3+7t\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262707 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186262402 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262707 #edb/ref 1069 "q-127078" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262707 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262707 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the parametric equations of the line $\\frac{x-10}{7}=\\frac{y+8}{-4}=\\frac{z+1}{11}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262707 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c2f75223-42f3-536a-93af-cb8a85108498" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262707 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the straight line that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y},{v}_{z}⟩$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}}=\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}}=\\frac{z-{z}_{0}}{{v}_{z}}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nComparing the above to our given equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-10}{7}=\\frac{y-(-8)}{-4}=\\frac{z-(-1)}{11},\n$$\n\nwe find that our line passes through the point $P(10,-8,-1)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨7,-4,11⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=10+7t \\\\ y=-8-4t \\\\ z=-1+11t\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263958 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10x+5y=-15 \\\\ 12x+3y=6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263958 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263958 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6e7865c0-26cb-5458-8cb7-a258df943633" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186264614 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{aligned}{\